  "description": "***No complete builds available. Framesets only.***\n\nEven the most dreaded of Monday mornings can be softened with the fun, fresh air, and blood-pumping exercise of commuting by bicycle. Realistically, you can ride any bike to the office, but we created the Beltline to be the ultimate commute to work—easy, quiet, and maintenance-free. With the Beltline, there are no more excuses.\n\nFeaturing the combination of a Gates carbon belt drive and an Alfine 8-speed internal hub, the drivetrain is durable, fast, and grease-free. The ride is impressively quiet and shifting is consistently smooth; you won’t run into any of the mess or frustrations of traditional bike chains and gears. The Beltline’s disc brake setup allows for supreme stopping in all types of commuting weather, an included dynamo front hub for a headlight, and the bike is centered in the comfort and responsiveness of American-made OX Platinum tubing.\n\nThough billed as the perfect commuter, the Beltline isn’t just anchored to the daily grind. It’s ideal for relaxing evening rides or Sunday trips to the beach or through the park. The Beltline is your everyday bike: take it out, take it far, take a day off and ride.\n\nFramesets Starting at $1,350.00\n\nFEATURES AND INFORMATION\nDesigned And Developed By Milwaukee Bicycle Co. - Handmade By the old Waterford Precision Cycles*\n\nTUBING\nThe Milwaukee Beltline is built featuring complete Vari-wall THERMLX main & rear end.\n\nTIRE CLEARANCE\nClearance for 700/650b 48c Tires.\n\nBRAKE CABLE ROUTING\nDown Tube Underside Zip Tie Brake Cable Routing.\n\nBRAZE-ONS\nSeat Tube and Down Tube Water Bottle Bosses\n\nFender/Rack Mounts\nDisc Brake Down Tube Cable Guides\nRear Alfine IGH Cable Stops\nISO Mount Disc Brake Only\nStainless Steel Milwaukee Headbadge, Milwaukee Script And WI State Badges\n\nS.H.I.S. Stem Clamp Diameter: 28.6",
